fixture toss_on_cling_frame_goes_away
doc docs/adr/0010, the wall and the Ember Toss "From a wall cling it goes away from the wall" (movement review 4, M5): the toss pressed with the stick toward the wall on the tick the fall reaches it and clings. A press on that tick is a press on the wall, so the ember goes away from it, as one thrown a tick later from the cling does (tech11_toss_from_cling_goes_away). (It used to be thrown into the wall, stop beside Ash and spend the 12 s cooldown.)
room test/shaft
spawn 760 300
frames 40
input
  0..5 R
  6 R toss
  7..39 R
end
expect
  at 6 event.wall_cling=1 state=wall event.toss=1
  # Away from the wall: the ember is left of Ash once it has flown.
  at 20 ember=1 ember_x<x@20
  at 20 ember_x<=-60u+x@20
end
